.code/contract \"v3\" :yin.k/version\n+0}` wherever this document shows it (§7.2's example `:121`, §7.2.1\n+`:183`, §7.3.3 `:232-236`) is the stack-shaped machine's; the\n+register-shaped machine's contract is `\"v4\"`\n+(`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §6), the one the version-3 profile map\n+names, and §7.2's envelope example is superseded for version 3 by the\n+row carrier's wire unit (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §3, ids under\n+Jing's default digest).\" The same grep (`legacy`, `version-0`,\n+`version 0`, `versions 0`, `version 1`, `recovery`) found, besides the\n+clauses above: the export-recovery object's version-1 format\n+(`:1789-1807`), which is phase 7's to re-base on the row carrier and is\n+named in §8.4 as an entry condition, not amended here; publication\n+failure recovery (`:1741`), completion recovery (`:2417`) and the\n+ledger's \"legacy destructive readers\" (`:2774-2775`), which concern the\n+driver, the ledger protocol and the ledger reader, not a body version,\n+and are untouched; and the status paragraph `:39-42`, covered by the\n+scope statement's \"every clause\".\n+\n ### 10.4 To code-as-tuples (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`) §7.2\n \n **C1 (ACCEPT).** Replace the first paragraph with: \"The vector-to-datoms\n@@ -1451,8 +1659,8 @@ remaining is owner-level.\n 1. **Nil-valued window keys (Dart, Node).** The window is built with\n    `select-keys` and encoded as `[r [:lit nil]]`; never filter `some?`\n    values; `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member` over row 22\n-   (`(f nil (next-of c))`, the nil operand evaluated before the read) is\n-   the canary. Membership is always by `contains?`/key sets, never\n+   (`(pair nil (next-of c))`, the nil operand evaluated before the read)\n+   is the canary. Membership is always by `contains?`/key sets, never\n    `(get W r)`.\n 2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\n    thousands of rows; build with `mapv`/`into`/`reduce`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files test | rg 'safepoint'; sed -n '842,853p' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc; sed -n '55,61p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '131,139p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/analysis_test.cljc; sed -n '310,333p' test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc; sed -n '56,104p' test/yin/vm/ucf/v2_support.cljc; sed -n '716,733p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc; sed -n '838,841p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files test | rg 'safepoint'; sed -n '842,853p' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc; sed -n '55,61p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '131,139p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/analysis_test.cljc; sed -n '310,333p' test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc; sed -n '56,104p' test/yin/vm/ucf/v2_support.cljc; sed -n '716,733p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc; sed -n '838,841p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"test/yang/safepoint_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_programs.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc\n(defn numeric-kind\n  \"The content kind of numeric x: :integer, :float64, :decimal or :rational.\n   Host integer width is not a kind: a long and a big integer of one value\n   are both :integer.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (host-integer? x) :integer\n    (float64? x) :float64\n    (decimal? x) :decimal\n    (ratio? x) :rational\n    :else (refuse :unsupported-value\n                  (str \"not a portable number: \" (type-name x)))))\n(defn bind-params\n  \"Zips params with args, nil-filling any params beyond args' length.\n   Extra args beyond params' length are dropped. §7.7.2: an under-arity\n   call leaves missing parameter names bound to nil, not absent.\"\n  [params args]\n  (into {} (map vector params (concat args (repeat nil)))))\n\n(deftest saved-window-of-a-non-tail-call\n  ;; (f (g x) y): while (g x) runs, f's register 1 must survive the call;\n  ;; at the resume pc 4, L = {1 2} and saved(4, 2) = {1}.\n  (let [v (:vector (get corpus/goldens :worked-example))\n        a (analysis/analyze v)]\n    (is (= #{1 2} (analysis/live a 4)))\n    (is (= #{1} (analysis/saved a 4 2)))\n    (is (= #{1 2 5} (analysis/live a 5)))\n    (is (= #{} (analysis/live a 0)))))\n(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n  \"A real machine parked at an explicit park whose module store for\n   'host.mod holds two cursor references nothing else reaches, named by\n   a module closure in the task store -- the shape a lowered module\n   closure has, its environment naming the module whose store it runs\n   against -- so the module-store snapshot's walk is the first place\n   either cell is minted.\"\n  []\n  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                            (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                                  (then (def! 'mod (lit 1))\n                                        (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park})\n                                             (v 'mod))))))\n        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n        seg (:segment (first (vals (:parked machine))))\n        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n                            {:type :closure, :params [], :entry 0,\n                             :segment seg,\n                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n    (assoc machine\n           :store (assoc (:store machine) 'mod clo)\n           :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1, 'd c2}})))\n\n\n(defn lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n\n\n(defn v\n  [n]\n  {:type :variable, :name n})\n\n\n(defn lam\n  [params body]\n  {:type :lambda, :params params, :body body})\n\n\n(defn app\n  [f & args]\n  {:type :application, :operator f, :operands (vec args)})\n\n\n(defn def!\n  [k val]\n  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit k) val))\n\n\n(defn then\n  [a b]\n  (app (lam ['_] b) a))\n\n\n(defn cursor-of\n  [source]\n  {:type :stream/cursor, :source source})\n\n\n(defn next-of\n  [source]\n  {:type :stream/next, :source source})\n\n\n(defn let1\n  [param init body]\n  (app (lam [param] body) init))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; One machine builder per profile\n;; =============================================================================\n\n      :call\n      (let [argc (nth inst 1), tail? (nth inst 2)\n            total (count stack)\n            f-pos (- total argc 1)\n            f (nth stack f-pos)\n            args (subvec stack (inc f-pos) total)\n            stack' (subvec stack 0 f-pos)]\n        (case (engine/operator-kind vm f)\n          :closure\n          (let [c (values/payload f)\n                locals (bind-positional (:arity c) args)\n                body-frames (conj (:frames c) locals)\n                continuation' (if tail?\n                                continuation\n                                (conj continuation\n                                      (cond-> {:return-pc (inc pc),\n                                               :frames frames,\n                                               :stack-base (count stack')}\n      :stream-next\n      (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/next {:cursor (peek stack)}) (pop stack))\n\n      ;; :stream-close -- the source stream ref on top; yields nil\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
