{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '225,240p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; sed -n '1780,1788p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; sed -n '1840,1848p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; sed -n '1138,1172p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"`:incomplete-install`, `:install-response`, `:incomplete-write`,\n`:reason-mismatch`, `:inconsistent-halt`, `:unaddressed-segment`,\n`:address-mismatch`, and, under version 1, `:unprotected-pending` and\n`:op-seq-exhausted` (7.4.3).\n\n**Two version keys.** `:yin.k/version` at the top of the body is the\nbody's own version and is what this amendment raises. The key of the\nsame name inside `:yin.k/contract` belongs to the code stamp of 7.3.3.\nThat stamp is compared whole and stays `{:yin.code/contract \"v3\"\n:yin.k/version 0}`: the amendment changes handoff data and composition\nadmission, not opcode semantics, so code stamps \"v3\", \"b2\" and \"r2\" and\nmodule manifest schema 1 are unchanged, and cursor vectors keep their\nbytes.\n\n**The version gate.** A resumer decodes the bytes, checks the tag, and\nthen checks the body version before any other rule. A version it does\n\nA `nil` header lifts today's version-0 fork; a header lifts version 1,\nexclusive, in the canonical codec, with `:yin.k/policy\n:yin.k/exclusive` added by the lift. The occurrence is minted once by\nthe driver and persisted before prepare is called; `:yin.k/enrolled`\nis the composition's declaration from the ledger reader; it is never\nencoded into the UCF body, but the header stays in the retained export\nrecord. The live record can contain authentic closures and is not itself\na canonical data object. `holder.export/freeze [machine prepared-record]`\nheader agree at lift: blocked and parked roots carry occurrence,\narbitration, counter and policy, and origin when present; a halted\nroot carries origin only, and a header-bearing halt without an origin\nis refused -- it is not automatically downgraded (a halt with no\norigin at all is a version-0 result under a `nil` header); install\nchildren carry no header. Before answering `:ok`, a version-1 root\nlift runs `checkpoint/inspect` on its own bytes and address, then\n`handoff/validate-body` on the decoded body; install children do not\nindependently undergo the root custody inspection. Any refusal\n    accordingly), gives equal root ids; a marker absent from the map is\n    a test failure.\n11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log\n    shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and\n    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n\n### 8.2 Slice 6b: full task transport and the harness on the reference lane\n\n**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: `lift-task`, `lower-task` (§7), the\npending rows' lift and lower, install children. **Files to create.**\n`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\n`:semantic-register` lane). The old harness file is not edited.\n\n**Depends on:** the explicit `:free-env` lift argument supplied by the\nharness (§6.3; the 4b retention seam is a named follow-up for the 4b\ntrack, not a 6b prerequisite); 4b stage 2 (FFI retained→sent restoration, link\nrequest/response/install preservation, install children, the\nevaluator's `IModuleKernel` linking methods: `link-format`,\n`spawn-module`, `lift-closure`, `lower-closure`); **phase 5c** (the\n`scan` namespace, for the dependency closure over `\"v4\"` vectors, §7.1).\nTouches nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**Acceptance (6b).**\n\n1. `every-row-every-segment-matches-the-reference`: rows 1-19, 21, 22\n   and 24 of §5.2 × four segments, plus row 20 once (outside the\n   wrappers, §5.2), on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6; counts\n   asserted (22 wrapped rows × 4 segments + 1 = 89 runs).\n2. `tail-states-carry-no-window`: rows 6, 9, 12, 20 lift to `:tail`\n   rows of three slots and lower to through-`K` delivery.\n3. `install-rows-carry-the-child`: rows 10-12; the child's kind and\n   phase as stated; no initialization on lower.\n4. `captures`: rows 14-16 round-trip; row 15's invocation after lower\n   delivers once into the captured `rd` and yields `:done`.\n5. `free-env-shadowing`: row 21 yields `99` after lower.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Q4Y0TR6E' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-11 10:54:49.800 xcodebuild[12456:55904253]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-11 10:54:50.096 xcodebuild[12456:55904252] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-x7O7h2FU' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-11 10:54:50.822 xcodebuild[12461:55904284]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-11 10:54:51.085 xcodebuild[12461:55904283] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n?? collab/1791730000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791730000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791730000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design.report.md\n?? collab/1791760000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/1791760000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791760000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791770000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-revise.claude-fable-5-1.s